ly well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as a know-it-all, hot temper. Also we have \"relatively weak leadership skills\" for D. Also \"arrogance\" etc.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution. Perhaps we can bring up Candidate B's strengths and concerns, or Candidate A. Since D already discussed, we could bring up B's strengths and concerns, comparing to C. Or we could bring up A's strengths. The goal is to cover all candidates before final recommendation. So we should introduce discussion of Candidate B or A. Let's bring up Candidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Concerns: weak memory for numbers (attention to detail), makes nasty remarks (crew cooperation, professional communication). We can argue that while B has strong reliability and stress handling, the communication issues are severe for crew cooperation, perhaps more problematic than C's communication issues? Or we could argue that B's strengths make him a viable alternative, but the nasty remarks are a red flag. So we might still support C but note B as a secondary.\n\nThus our vote remains Candidate C. Provide evidence: B's strengths and concerns, compare to C. Conclude C still best.\n\nWe must output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. METADATA_JSON: {\"agent\":\"agent_2\",\"vote\":\"Candidate C\"}\n\nNow craft PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with the previous points and would still recommend Candidate C. While Candidate B shows strong reliability and stress handling, his tendency to make nasty remarks undermines crew cooperation, which is a critical safety factor. In contrast, C's communication issues, though present, are less severe and can be mitigated. Therefore, C remains the best fit.\"\n\nAdd mention of B's strengths: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills. And concerns: weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks.\n\nMake sure to reference prior discussion: \"I agree with Agent 1 and Agent 3...\"\n\nProceed."}
